closure label, ghc_hs_iface,"] [73 3 "// stable_ptr_table (rtsapi.go)"] [87 2 "// NODES.adjust: \"STUB INDEX\" a line, the parameter of the x86-64 adjustor's return address (bin/lib/hsi/check)"] [107 2 "// a function the C calls and neither it nor musl defines: hsi's own when its table has it (the RTS's API a test's C"] [108 2 "// calls: hs_free_stable_ptr, getProgArgv, ...)"] [123 1 "// RunC runs a -no-hs-main program (HES60 (a)): its C main through musl's __libc_start_main, which calls exit(main(argc,"] [124 1 "// argv, envp)); the C calls hs_init, its foreign exports (rts_inCall) and hs_exit, which flushes the Haskell handles as"] [125 1 "// hs_exit does. The status is the C's exit status."] [143 1 "// hsExit is hs_exit: the standard handles flushed (on a thread of their own, as shutdown's), the C finalizers run."] [150 3 "// the threaded RTS's hs_exit (exitScheduler, threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in safe foreign calls"] [151 3 "// left to return into a stopped RTS (conc059), where the non-threaded RTS's waits for them"] [160 1 "// cStack is an initial stack's vector as Linux's (ci's RunMain's): argv's pointers, 0, the environment's, 0, the"] [161 1 "// auxiliary vector (AT_PAGESZ, AT_RANDOM); the environment's address and argv[0]'s."] [187 1 "// cFunc is the C program's function named s when it defines one (code, or a native ci has)."] [199 1 "// cResolve is the C function a static foreign call of s calls when the C program has it and hsi's table does not, or"] [200 1 "// it is one of cFirst's."] [208 1 "// cFuncAt is the C program's function at address a, or nil."] [220 1 "// cCall calls f with the machine's argument values (an integer kind or an address as an integer, a float or a double as"] [221 1 "// a floating value) and returns its result in the representation res."] [248 1 "// cCallArgs calls f on ci's main thread."] [253 1 "// cNative makes hsi's C function fn at address a a native of ci's program: its arguments as the machine's values."] [258 1 "// cBridge makes f, a function of ci's program, call hsi's fn."] [282 1 "// cLabel is the address of the C program's object or function s, when it has one."] [296 1 "// cFlush flushes C's stdio at the program's end (libc's exit, after the Haskell handles' flush)."] [304 1 "// cValue is the value of the C program's object s in the representation res, when it has one: a capi import of a value"] [305 1 "// (foreign import capi \"h.h value i\"), whose wrapper GHC's C compiler makes and hsi reads as the object itself."] [329 1 "// identity is the word that stands for a heap object in memory C reads (an Array# argument's elements): a pinned byte"] [330 1 "// array's address, an integer itself, else an address of an unmapped region, one per object, kept for the run."] [355 1 "// identBase is the region of objects' identities: no mapping of crt's is there."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[54 20] [59 24] [61 29] [64 29] [65 46] [66 26] [74 24] [75 53] [89 44] [93 39] [111 29] [116 34] [128 20] [287 25] [290 43] [347 25]]} (go/file "cprog.go" :imports [


